{"name":"Golden Lake","hex":"#d8c7a2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"lake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, landlocked stretch of water or similar liquid.","A large amount of liquid."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An offering, sacrifice, gift.","Play; sport; game; fun; glee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden Lake","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Lake is a body of water located in Renfrew County Ontario, located on the Bonnechere River approximately 25 km southwest of Pembroke, Ontario. It is bounded by the Township of North Algona-Wilberforce, the Township of Bonnechere Valley and Algonquins of Pikwàkanagàn First Nation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Golden_Lake_Ontario.jpg/330px-Golden_Lake_Ontario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Lake","wikidata":"Q5579619"},{"title":"Golden Lake (Minnesota)","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Lake is a lake in Anoka County, Minnesota, in the United States."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Lake_(Minnesota)","wikidata":"Q19880597"},{"title":"Lake","blocks":[{"text":"A lake is often a naturally occurring, relatively large and fixed body of water on or near the Earth's surface. It is localized in a basin or interconnected basins surrounded by dry land. Lakes lie completely on land and are separate from the ocean, although they may be connected with the ocean by outflowing rivers. Lakes, like other bodies of water, are part of the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Most lakes are fresh water and account for almost all the world's surface freshwater, but some are salt lakes with salinities even higher than that of seawater. Lakes vary significantly in surface area and volume of water, but in total cover approximately 2.5 × 106 km2 (less than 2%) of the Earth's surface."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Lake_Idro_Italy_2005-08-16.jpg/330px-Lake_Idro_Italy_2005-08-16.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake","wikidata":"Q23397"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Sunset_at_nordhouse_dunes.jpg/500px-Sunset_at_nordhouse_dunes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Sunset_at_nordhouse_dunes.jpg/500px-Sunset_at_nordhouse_dunes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sunset over Lake Michigan at Nordhouse Dunes in Manistee National Forest, Michigan, United States","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunset_at_nordhouse_dunes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Castiglione_del_Lago%2C_Lago_Trasimeno.jpg/500px-Castiglione_del_Lago%2C_Lago_Trasimeno.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Castiglione_del_Lago%2C_Lago_Trasimeno.jpg/1280px-Castiglione_del_Lago%2